Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: order Elden video-mode teardown flush before timing stop
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On lenovo,elden the master and slave video encoders drive one split
pipeline. Stopping the compositor gracefully disables the interface and
lets the DPU/DSI blocks be torn down and re-enabled, after which the
panel stays black even though every register reads back as programmed:
the SSPP fetch never restarts and the layer mixer keeps emitting its
border colour.

dpu_encoder_helper_phys_cleanup() ends in a CTL flush, and in video mode
a flush is only consumed at a frame boundary. Running the cleanup after
enable_timing(0) therefore leaves the teardown in the shadow registers,
and the next enable inherits the stale active configuration. The flush
must be issued while the timing engine is still running, so the Elden
master now calls the cleanup before stopping the timing engine and no
longer repeats it at the end of the function.

The Elden slave shares the master's CTL and timing generator, so it skips
the teardown entirely and only transitions to DISABLED. Its matching
enable half in dpu_encoder_phys_vid_handle_post_kickoff() marks the slave
ENABLED without starting the timing engine a second time.

The paired enable/disable contract is taken from h0cheung's tb322fc tree,
commit 6f97250ead155fc3b980856323e99a4623dae73d, narrowed to this board;
every other machine keeps the existing ordering, the existing cleanup
placement and the existing kickoff path verbatim. This is patch 0153; it
is meant to be applied on top of 0152.

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
---

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
@@ -601,6 +601,7 @@
 	unsigned long lock_flags;
 	int ret;
 	struct dpu_hw_intf_status intf_status = {0};
+	bool is_elden = of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,elden");
 
 	if (!phys_enc->parent || !phys_enc->parent->dev) {
 		DPU_ERROR("invalid encoder/device\n");
@@ -621,6 +622,25 @@
 		return;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * On Elden the master and slave interfaces are two halves of one video
+	 * pipeline; only the master owns the shared CTL flush and the timing
+	 * generator, so the slave has nothing to stop or clean up.
+	 */
+	if (is_elden && !dpu_encoder_phys_vid_is_master(phys_enc))
+		goto done;
+
+	/*
+	 * On Elden the teardown must be flushed while the timing engine is
+	 * still running. The cleanup ends in a CTL flush, and video mode only
+	 * consumes a flush at a frame boundary, so a flush issued after the
+	 * timing engine has stopped stays in the shadow registers and the next
+	 * enable inherits a stale active configuration: the SSPP fetch never
+	 * restarts and the layer mixer keeps emitting its border colour.
+	 */
+	if (is_elden)
+		dpu_encoder_helper_phys_cleanup(phys_enc);
+
 	spin_lock_irqsave(phys_enc->enc_spinlock, lock_flags);
 	phys_enc->hw_intf->ops.enable_timing(phys_enc->hw_intf, 0);
 	if (dpu_encoder_phys_vid_is_master(phys_enc))
@@ -665,7 +685,9 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	dpu_encoder_helper_phys_cleanup(phys_enc);
+	if (!is_elden)
+		dpu_encoder_helper_phys_cleanup(phys_enc);
+done:
 	phys_enc->enable_state = DPU_ENC_DISABLED;
 }
 
@@ -673,12 +695,22 @@
 		struct dpu_encoder_phys *phys_enc)
 {
 	unsigned long lock_flags;
+	bool is_elden = of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,elden");
 
 	/*
 	 * Video mode must flush CTL before enabling timing engine
 	 * Video encoders need to turn on their interfaces now
 	 */
 	if (phys_enc->enable_state == DPU_ENC_ENABLING) {
+		/*
+		 * The Elden slave is driven by the master's timing engine;
+		 * starting it here would restart the generator a second time.
+		 */
+		if (is_elden && !dpu_encoder_phys_vid_is_master(phys_enc)) {
+			phys_enc->enable_state = DPU_ENC_ENABLED;
+			return;
+		}
+
 		trace_dpu_enc_phys_vid_post_kickoff(DRMID(phys_enc->parent),
 				    phys_enc->hw_intf->idx - INTF_0);
 		spin_lock_irqsave(phys_enc->enc_spinlock, lock_flags);
